# Ticket Schema

Provider-agnostic schema for infrastructure requests. Supported providers: **jira** | **linear** | **pasted**.

Team/project key: **PE** (Platform Engineering) by default (`JIRA_PROJECT_KEY` / `LINEAR_TEAM_KEY`). Pasted requests use `PE-paste-<service>` when the user does not supply a key.

## Required fields

| Field | Format | Example |
|-------|--------|---------|
| Summary / Title | `{action} {service} to Vault` | Onboard payments-api to Vault |
| Service name | kebab-case | payments-api |
| Team | lowercase | payments |
| Environment | local/staging/prod | local |
| K8s namespace | lowercase | payments |
| K8s service account | matches service or dedicated SA | payments-api |
| Secret paths | comma-separated | config, db |
| Approver | username | platform-lead |
| Acceptance criteria | free text | Service can read config and db secrets |

## Where fields live (per provider)

### Pasted (no tracker)

Paste the field list into Cursor Agent chat (Ultra / local). Skill: `onboard-from-paste`. Set `ticket_provider: pasted`. No MCP.

### Jira

- Prefer custom fields on issue type **Infrastructure Request** (or Task with labels).
- Jira Free workaround: use labels `service:payments-api`, `team:payments`, `namespace:payments`, `sa:payments-api`, `secrets:config,db`.

### Linear

- Put structured fields in the issue **description** as a markdown table or bullet list with the field names above.
- Also apply labels: `service:payments-api`, `team:payments`, `namespace:payments`, `sa:payments-api`, `secrets:config,db`.
- Issue type / label: `infrastructure-request` (optional but recommended).

## Rejection criteria

Reject tickets missing service name, team, namespace, service account, or secret paths. Ask requester to update before writing spec.
